Read mke2fs.conf and e2fsck.conf from /etc.

configure substitutes ROOT_SYSCONFDIR with the install prefix, a store
path that exists on no user's machine, so mke2fs fell back to its
compiled-in defaults instead of the distribution's filesystem profiles.
The template is patched, not the make variable: the value is baked at
configure time, and the install itself stays in the prefix.

--- a/lib/dirpaths.h.in
+++ b/lib/dirpaths.h.in
@@ -7,4 +7,4 @@
 #define LOCALEDIR		"@datadir@/locale"
 
 /* Where to find the mke2fs.conf and e2fsck.conf files */
-#define ROOT_SYSCONFDIR		"@root_sysconfdir@"
+#define ROOT_SYSCONFDIR		"/etc"
